---
const customers = [[10,1,'Mina Shah'],[10,2,'Tariq Aziz'],[10,3,'Edda Berg'],[20,4,'Rowan Vale']];
---
<figure class="access-figure" id="access-row-model" aria-labelledby="access-row-caption">
  <figcaption id="access-row-caption"><span class="access-number">Figure 2</span> Existing rows and proposed rows</figcaption>
  <div class="access-panel">
    <p class="access-kicker">shop_runtime · authorised context 10</p>
    <pre class="access-query" data-query data-live>SELECT customer_id, name FROM shop.customers;</pre>
    <label class="access-option">Statement <select data-command><option value="all">Read all customers</option><option value="rowan">Read customer 4</option><option value="hidden">Update customer 4</option><option value="move">Move order 103 to tenant 20</option></select></label>
    <p class="access-kicker">Ordinary object privileges: allowed in every case</p>
    <div class="access-gates access-direct-gates" aria-label="Policy checks">
      <div class="access-gate"><b>USING · existing rows</b><span data-using data-live>Tenant 10 admits 1, 2 and 3; hides 4</span></div>
      <div class="access-gate"><b>WITH CHECK · proposed rows</b><span data-check data-live>No proposed row in this SELECT</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="access-row-grid" data-rows data-live data-customers={JSON.stringify(customers)}>{customers.map(([tenant,id,name]) => <div class:list={['access-row',{'access-excluded':tenant!==10}]}><b>{id} · {name}</b><span>Tenant {tenant} · {tenant===10?'admitted':'outside result'}</span></div>)}</div>
    <p class="access-result" data-result data-live>3 rows · Mina, Tariq and Edda</p>
    <p class="access-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">The result contains customers 1, 2 and 3. The missing application condition did not expose Rowan.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="access-caption">A model of the policies described here, not a trace of their physical evaluation order. Customer rows stay stored when filtered out. Both update attempts leave the three starting orders unchanged.</p>
  <details><summary>Figure as text</summary><p>All four statements have the required ordinary privileges. With context 10, reading all customers returns Mina, Tariq and Edda; customer 4 is hidden. Updating customer 4’s name to itself affects zero rows under context 10, because Rowan’s existing tenant-20 row is hidden. Order 103 has tenant 10, so USING admits it. Changing its tenant to 20 fails WITH CHECK and rejects the statement before a new row is stored.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
  const root = document.querySelector('#access-row-model');
  if (root) {
    const select = root.querySelector('[data-command]');
    const put = (selector, value) => { root.querySelector(selector).textContent = value; };
    const customers = JSON.parse(root.querySelector('[data-rows]').getAttribute('data-customers'));
    const cases = {
      all: {query:'SELECT customer_id, name FROM shop.customers;', using:'Tenant 10 admits 1, 2 and 3; hides 4', check:'No proposed row in this SELECT', result:'3 rows · Mina, Tariq and Edda', explanations:['The query has no tenant condition. Context 10 has already been established by the trusted service.','SELECT permits reading the requested columns. It does not choose the rows.','USING admits the three tenant-10 rows. Rowan remains stored but is outside this result.','The result contains customers 1, 2 and 3. The missing application condition did not expose Rowan.']},
      rowan: {query:'SELECT customer_id, name FROM shop.customers\nWHERE customer_id = 4;',using:'Rowan has tenant 20 · hidden',check:'No proposed row in this SELECT',result:'0 rows · customer 4 is outside the policy',explanations:['The request names customer 4, Rowan Vale. Knowing this key supplies no permission.','The ordinary SELECT privilege is present, so a missing grant does not explain the outcome.','Rowan’s tenant 20 fails USING with context 10. The query condition cannot widen that allowance.','The result is empty. This says nothing about whether Rowan exists for another authorised identity.']},
      hidden: {query:'UPDATE shop.customers SET name = name\nWHERE customer_id = 4;',using:'Customer 4 · tenant 20 · hidden',check:'No proposed row reaches this check',result:'UPDATE 0 · no stored change',explanations:['This diagnostic statement proposes leaving customer 4’s name unchanged. The existing Rowan row makes the boundary test visible.','The fixture grants UPDATE on name and SELECT on the needed columns for this probe. Before RLS the same statement affects one row.','USING permits tenant-10 customers only. Rowan’s existing tenant-20 row is hidden from the update.','UPDATE 0 records the filtered target. No proposed row reaches WITH CHECK. The name remains Rowan Vale.']},
      move: {query:'UPDATE shop.orders SET tenant_id = 20\nWHERE order_id = 103;',using:'Order 103 · tenant 10 · admitted',check:'Proposed tenant 20 ≠ context 10 · rejected',result:'ERROR 42501 · no stored change',explanations:['Order 103 starts in tenant 10 and is pending. This is an attempted tenant change, not a completed migration.','The ordinary UPDATE and SELECT privileges are present.','USING admits existing order 103 because its tenant is 10. A read filter alone would not reject its proposed tenant.','WITH CHECK tests the proposed row. Tenant 20 fails, so PostgreSQL rejects the statement before storing it. Separate integrity rules still apply to permitted proposals.']}
    };
    const draw = () => {
      const mode = select.value; const item = cases[mode];
      put('[data-query]',item.query);
      put('[data-using]',item.using); put('[data-check]',item.check);
      put('[data-result]',item.result); put('[data-explanation]',item.explanations[3]);
      const host=root.querySelector('[data-rows]'); host.replaceChildren();
      const data=mode==='move'?[[10,103,'Pending order']]:customers;
      for(const [tenant,id,name] of data) {
        const card=document.createElement('div'); card.className='access-row';
        const visible=tenant===10&&(mode!=='rowan'||id===4)&&(mode!=='hidden'||id===4);
        card.classList.toggle('access-excluded',!visible);
        const nameNode=document.createElement('b'); nameNode.textContent=`${id} · ${name}`;
        const detail=document.createElement('span'); detail.textContent=`Tenant ${tenant} · ${visible?'admitted':'outside result'}`;
        card.append(nameNode,detail); host.append(card);
      }
    };
    select.addEventListener('change',draw); draw();
  }
</script>
<style>
  .access-direct-gates { grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:.6rem; }
  @media(max-width:600px) { .access-direct-gates { grid-template-columns:1fr; } }
</style>
